  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Friday)\nIssued at 1050 AM CST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nPacific shortwave will move ESE across the Rockies Saturday and\npass near the local area Sat night into Sunday. Winds will further\nincrease from the south ahead of the wave Saturday, though an\noverall increase in clouds will temper additional warming\noverall. Winds will maintain a limited grassfire spread potential,\nhowever should see higher dewpoints begin to spread north by \nthen.\n\nFast movement of system will likely prevent much deep moisture \nreturn in advance of the wave, with thunder potential remaining \nquite limited as a result. Strong cold front will quickly move \nthrough Saturday night with a period of strong and gusty northwest\nwinds behind it. Some gusts approaching advisory level (40 mph) \nseem likely and if additional data supports any increase in wind \ngusts, an advisory may be needed for parts of the area. Some light\nrain showers expected in wrap around band into Sunday morning and\nat this point, thermal profiles continue to favor liquid until \nafter any precip moves out.\n\nFast westerly flow will bring south winds back quickly next week \nwith a resultant warmup to well above normal temps by mid week. A\nstronger system continues to be depicted in medium range models \ntoward the end of the week, this time with more notable moisture \nreturn suggested.",
